ChatGLM package-owned model and tokenizer adaptations

ChatGLM2/3 source: THUDM / Tsinghua University, 2023.
GLM-4 source: Zhipu AI, 2024.
Adaptations for GPT-QModel / Transformers 5: ModelCloud.ai, 2026.

Code is distributed under the Apache License 2.0, retained in LICENSE and
LICENSE.glm4. The model rotary helper also retains the labml.ai MIT notice in
LICENSE.rope. No trained model weights are included; checkpoint weight licenses
remain separate. Immutable model/tokenizer revisions, source hashes, tokenizer
asset hashes and adaptation details are recorded in PROVENANCE.md,
checkpoint_contracts.json and tokenizer_contracts.json.

SentencePiece and TikToken are separately installed dependencies, not vendored
here. Tests fetch only the hash-pinned tokenizer data assets; runtime never
downloads or imports checkpoint Python.
